        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Mumbai</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 250 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">People lived on the islands from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stone-age">Stone Age</a>, and the islands became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> in the 3rd century BCE; the Koli fishing community had long inhabited them.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on what was originally an archipelago of seven islands with a deep natural harbour on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>, in the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A harbour of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a>; the Kanheri Caves and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elephanta-caves">Elephanta Caves</a>; Portuguese and then British Bombay; the Hornby Vellard; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s first passenger railway; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> mills and trade; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a> and the independence movement; Bollywood</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Mumbai is the capital of the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> and a city of more than 12 million people.</span></div>
